    "line": 117,
    "published": "The decisive finding is the seam attribution, exactly as preregistered in plan 4.2/9.4: the PIT-clean anchor fails G2 (PF 1.033/1.051 vs 1.20), G3 (3/6 positive folds) and G4 (net < 0 at k=1.5) on BOTH pairs, while its one-day-lookahead twin R-ORIG passes ALL EIGHT gates on BOTH pairs (AUDUSD +3207.4 net, PF 1.380, 5/6 folds, +2232.5 @1.5; USDCAD +5029.6, PF 1.428, 5/6 folds, +3838.9 @1.5). All three seam limbs fire on both pairs (S = 2884.1 and 4348.6 pips vs thresholds 20.0/24.0; per-trip matched deltas 8.05/12.96 pips vs 1*c_rt 2.0/2.4 on 337/306 matched pairs): **the apparent range-expansion edge on these pairs was the PIT seam, not economics**. The edge also fails cost stress violently (net flips negative at k=1.5 on both pairs; ~2100/2400 pips of round-trip cost against ~2300/3100 pips gross), the clock-placebo loses money outright (-2207.3/-978.3), and the inverted control wins on folds where the anchor loses (KILL_INVERSION) \u2014 the sign carried no mechanism. The one-look holdout windows (2026-01-01..2026-06-30) were consumed by NOBODY and remain unread for any future re-derivation.",
